    "formContent": "<div class=\"ielts-form-container\"><div class=\"form-section\"><div class=\"form-title\" style=\"text-align:center;font-weight:700;font-size:1.1em;margin-bottom:8px;\">Sources of rubber</div><p style=\"font-weight:700;\">Three resources which are essential for industrial civilisation</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"31\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"></p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; fossil fuels</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; rubber</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Natural rubber</p><p>This mainly comes from the Para rubber tree, now cultivated in South-East Asia.</p><p>The supply is limited because</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; the growth of the tree is <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"32\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; production cannot easily be adjusted because of increasing or decreasing <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"33\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; the tree only grows near the <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"34\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; extracting the latex (rubber) is labour-intensive</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; it is very difficult to <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"35\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> rubber after production.</p><p style=\"margin-top:6px;\">New threats include</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; lack of genetic diversity, leading to danger of disease caused by a <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"36\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; a shift to the cultivation of palm oil</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; extreme <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"37\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> events.</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">Synthetic rubber</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; may be used for engine parts and cooking utensils</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; is less <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"38\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> than natural rubber</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; is unsuitable for many purposes e.g. the tyres of aircraft.</p><p style=\"font-weight:700;margin-top:10px;\">An alternative source of natural rubber</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; A wild flower (a type of dandelion) has rubber in its <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"39\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p><p style=\"padding-left:18px;\">&bull;&nbsp; It can be grown in many locations and does not require good <input type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" class=\"gap-input\" data-q=\"40\" style=\"width:130px;text-align:center;\"> .</p></div></div>",
